course: dictionary
lesson: 11712
title: Auld, a Scots word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one part of the world, and they still mean something real. «Auld» is a Scots word, used in Scotland and parts of Northern Ireland. It means old. «The auld castle stood on the hill for hundreds of years.» Here, auld means old, just like the castle is old.
explain: You will often hear auld in songs and poems. The famous song «Auld Lang Syne» is by the Scottish poet Robert Burns. Its title means something like «old long since», or days long ago. People sing it at New Year, holding hands in a circle, all over the English-speaking world.
explain: Context helps you here too. «My auld gran has a tartan blanket older than my mum.» The word gran tells you it is a person, and older than my mum gives the clue: auld means old, so the gran is old.
fact: «Auld» means old. It is a Scots word.
fact: Auld is used in Scotland and Northern Ireland, in songs, poems and everyday talk.
fact: «Auld Lang Syne» is a Scottish song by Robert Burns, and it means days long ago.
fact: People sing «Auld Lang Syne» at New Year, which is called Hogmanay in Scotland.
fact: «Auld Reekie», meaning «Old Smoky», is a nickname for Edinburgh.
exercise: «The auld castle stood on the hill for hundreds of years.» What does auld mean? | Wet | Tiny | *Old | New
exercise: What does «Auld Lang Syne» mean? | *Days long ago | Dinner for the family | A football match | A trip to the seaside
exercise: «My auld gran has a tartan blanket older than my mum.» Which word tells you that auld means old? | tartan | blanket | *older | gran
test: «Our auld dog still loves a walk, even though he is ten.» What does auld mean here? | *Old | Lost | Brand new | Very loud
test: Auld Reekie is a nickname for which city? | Belfast | London | *Edinburgh | Glasgow
exam: In «Auld Lang Syne», the words mean «old long since». What is the best meaning? | A happy dance | A cold winter night | A new year party | *Old, long since, meaning days long ago
